stdout | Parse files in project and emit diagnostics, optionally apply fixes
stdout |
stdout | Usage: elp lint [OPTIONS]
stdout |
stdout | Options:
stdout |       --project <PROJECT>              Path to directory with project, or to a JSON file [default:
stdout |                                        .]
stdout |       --module <MODULE>                Parse a single module from the project, not the entire
stdout |                                        project
stdout |       --app <APP>                      Parse a single application from the project, not the entire
stdout |                                        project
stdout |       --file <FILE>                    Parse one or more files from the project, not the entire
stdout |                                        project. This can be an include file or escript, etc
stdout |       --path <PATH>                    Only process files under this path (can be a file or
stdout |                                        directory)
stdout |       --ignore-app <APP>               Skip the given application. Can be repeated to skip several
stdout |       --rebar                          Run with rebar
stdout |       --as <PROFILE>                   Rebar3 profile to pickup [default: test]
stdout |       --connect                        Use the persistent daemon for fast turnaround (default when
stdout |                                        watchman is installed; auto-starts if needed). Pass
stdout |                                        --no-connect to disable
stdout |       --no-connect                     Disable the persistent daemon and run standalone (no
stdout |                                        cross-run caching)
stdout |       --include-generated              Also generate diagnostics for generated files
stdout |       --include-tests                  Deprecated (no-op): Diagnostics for test files are now always
stdout |                                        included
stdout |       --no-diags                       Do not print the full diagnostics for a file, just the count
stdout |       --format <FORMAT>                Customize the output format (defaults to human-readable)
stdout |                                        [possible values: json]
stdout |       --include-erlc-diagnostics       Include diagnostics produced by erlc
stdout |       --include-ct-diagnostics         Deprecated (no-op): Common Test diagnostics are now always
stdout |                                        included
stdout |       --include-eqwalizer-diagnostics  Include Eqwalizer diagnostics
stdout |       --include-suppressed             Include Suppressed diagnostics (e.g. elp:fixme)
stdout |       --use-cli-severity               If specified, use the provided CLI severity mapping instead
stdout |                                        of the default one
stdout |       --severity <SEVERITY>            Minimum severity level to report [possible values: error,
stdout |                                        warning, weak_warning, information]
stdout |       --diagnostic-ignore <CODE>       Ignore the specified diagnostic, by code or label. Can be
stdout |                                        repeated to ignore several diagnostics
stdout |       --diagnostic-filter <CODE>       Filter out all reported diagnostics except the specified
stdout |                                        one(s), by code or label. Can be repeated to keep several
stdout |                                        diagnostics
stdout |       --experimental                   Report experimental diagnostics too, if diagnostics are
stdout |                                        enabled
stdout |       --read-config                    Deprecated and now a no-op: the project's .elp_lint.toml is
stdout |                                        read by default. Use --config-file to override the config
stdout |                                        file
stdout |       --config-file <CONFIG_FILE>      Override the lint configuration file (.elp_lint.toml) used
stdout |       --apply-fix                      If the diagnostic has an associated fix, apply it. Modifies
stdout |                                        the original file. Use --to to write to a different directory
stdout |       --ignore-fix-only                Only apply elp:ignore fixes
stdout |       --fixme-fix-only                 Only apply elp:fixme fixes
stdout |       --to <TO>                        When applying a fix, put the results in this directory path
stdout |       --recursive                      If applying fixes, apply any new ones that arise from the
stdout |                                        prior fixes recursively. Limited in scope to the clause of
stdout |                                        the prior change
stdout |       --with-check                     After applying a fix step, check that the diagnostics are
stdout |                                        clear, else roll back
stdout |       --check-eqwalize-all             After applying a fix step, check that all eqwalizer project
stdout |                                        diagnostics are clear, else roll back
stdout |       --one-shot                       Apply to all matching diagnostic occurrences at once, rather
stdout |                                        than one at a time
stdout |       --arc-patch                      When using --format=json, populate original/replacement
stdout |                                        fields with fix information for arc lint auto-fix support
stdout |       --report-system-stats            Report system memory usage and other statistics
stdout |       --no-stream                      Disable streaming of diagnostics when applying fixes (collect
stdout |                                        all before printing)
stdout |   -h, --help                           Print help
stdout |
stdout | Global options:
stdout |       --log-file <LOG_FILE>  
stdout |       --erl <ERL>            
stdout |       --escript <ESCRIPT>    
stdout |       --no-log-buffering     
stdout |       --no-buck-generated    Deprecated (no-op): buck project loading always builds generated code
stdout |       --buck-quick-start     Deprecated (no-op): buck project loading always builds generated code
stdout |       --color <WHEN>         Use color in output [default: always] [possible values: always, never,
stdout |                              auto]
